    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Find your way",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "14pt",
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#1478BE"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "• The tabs in the dark bar: Home (the headline figures), Story (one sentence and one chart for each area), Scorecard (every KPI and its status), Details (six pages, opened with the buttons beside the Month slicer), Data quality and Guide.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#0A1E32"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "• How to use and Definitions, top right, open this Guide.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#0A1E32"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "• On the Scorecard, select a row and use Drill through to KPI detail for its trend, hospitals and definition. Right-click a hospital or department bar and choose Drill through > Employee list for the people behind a number. Back, beside the Month slicer, returns to the page you came from.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#0A1E32"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "• Hospital and Month carry over to every page. Month opens on Last closed month, the month just ended; pick another month in the list to see it.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#0A1E32"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "• The sentences on Story and the figures on the cards describe the one month you picked. The trend charts always show the last 12 closed months, whatever Month says.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#0A1E32"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "• Period, on Scorecard and KPI detail, reads each KPI for the month (Current), the quarter to date (QTD) or the year to date (YTD) up to the month you picked. Annual targets of rates such as turnover are pro-rated to the months; month-end figures such as headcount stay at the month end.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#0A1E32"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "• Story rates show 2 decimals because monthly rates are small. The largest change names the hospital whose rate or number moved most.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "12pt",
                      "color": "#0A1E32"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
